/* book Worked example 2: Q: The beam of the first singly reinforced example (230 × 450 mm, 3 bars of 20 mm, Cmin = 38 mm to the main bars, d = 402 mm, M25) carries a service moment of 75 kN·m. Find the crack width at the bottom corner, taking m = 280/(3σcbc) = 10.98 for M25 (σcbc = 8.5 N/mm²).
   1. Cracked neutral axis: 230 x²/2 = 10.98 × 942.5 × (402 − x), so x = 150.5 mm. Icr = 230 × 150.5³/3 + 10.98 × 942.5 × 251.5² = 9.16 × 10⁸ mm⁴.
   2. Steel stress fs = 10.98 × 75 × 10⁶ × 251.5/(9.16 × 10⁸) = 226.2 N/mm², steel strain 226.2/200 000 = 0.001131.
   3. Strain at the soffit: ε1 = 0.001131 × (450 − 150.5)/(402 − 150.5) = 0.001347.
   4. εm = 0.001347 − 230 × 299.5 × 299.5/(3 × 200 000 × 942.5 × 251.5) = 0.001347 − 0.000145 = 0.001202.
   5. Bar centres are 48 mm from the side and the soffit, so at the corner acr = √(48² + 48²) − 10 = 57.9 mm.
   6. wcr = 3 × 57.9 × 0.001202/[1 + 2 × (57.9 − 38)/(450 − 150.5)] = 0.2088/1.133 = 0.18 mm.
   7. Detailing check: clear spacing 47 mm, far less than 180 mm for Fe415.
   Answer: wcr = 0.18 mm at the corner, inside the 0.3 mm general limit and the 0.2 mm limit for exposed members. */
